    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "Marking legibility test: Observer, with a visual acuity of 0 on the log Minimum Angle of Resolution (log MAR) scale or 6/6 (20/20) and is able to read N6 of the Jaeger test card in normal room lighting condition (~500lx), reads marking at ambient illuminance least favourable level in the range of 100 lx to 1,500 lx. The ME EQUIPMENT or its part was positioned so that the viewpoint was the intended position of the OPERATOR or if not defined at any point within the base of a cone subtended by an angle of 30° to the axis normal to the centre of the plane of the marking and at a distance of 1 m.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "marking legibility",
        "visual acuity",
        "ambient illuminance",
        "log MAR",
        "IEC60601-1 clause 7.1.2"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "7.1.2 Legibility of Marking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "Durability of marking test procedure: Marking rubbed by hand, first for 15 s with a cloth rag soaked with distilled water, then for 15 s with a cloth rag soaked with ethanol 96%, and then for 15 s with a cloth rag soaked with isopropyl alcohol.",
